Enabling object-oriented access involves three main components: creating the userdata, setting up the metatable, and registering the methods.
1. Creating the Method Table and Metatable
Using Lua's auxiliary library, a unique metatable is created in the Lua registry using luaL_newmetatable. This metatable serves as both the class definition and the method repository.
// Define the methods exposed to Lua static const struct luaL_Reg mylib_methods[] = { {"get_value", mylib_get_value}, {"set_value", mylib_set_value}, {"close", mylib_destroy}, {NULL, NULL} }; int luaopen_mylib(lua_State *L) { // Create the metatable for the object type luaL_newmetatable(L, "MyLib.Object"); // Register methods into the metatable luaL_setfuncs(L, mylib_methods, 0); // Set metatable.__index = metatable lua_pushvalue(L, -1); lua_setfield(L, -2, "__index"); return 1; }
